## Validation & Testing

The BMS architecture was tested under multiple simulated fault conditions.

### Protection Testing

Individual fault conditions were injected into the battery model to verify:

- Over-temperature detection
- Cell over-voltage detection
- Cell under-voltage detection
- Over-current detection
- Cell imbalance detection
- Low-SOC detection
- Fault-code generation
- Fault-action response

### State Machine Testing

The following state transitions were validated:

- OFF → INITIALIZE
- INITIALIZE → PRECHARGE
- PRECHARGE → IDLE
- IDLE → CHARGING
- CHARGING → IDLE
- IDLE → DISCHARGING
- DISCHARGING → IDLE
- Fault → FAULT state
- Fault recovery after reset

### Precharge Testing

The precharge circuit was tested using the DC-link voltage feedback.

The system transitions from PRECHARGE to IDLE once the DC-link voltage reaches the required fraction of pack voltage.

A precharge timeout mechanism is also implemented to detect unsuccessful precharge.

### Cell Balancing Testing

Unequal cell conditions were introduced to verify the balancing controller.

The controller successfully identified the highest-voltage cell and activated its corresponding balancing path.
